# Cyclopean Tomb's land is stripped of its mire counter by Vampire Hexmage (a removal "with" Hexmage, not with the Tomb) before the
# Tomb dies. The text asks only that no mire counter "has been removed from [the land] with this artifact", so in the first upkeep
# after the Tomb is gone the Forest is still the one land to choose, and choosing it removes no counter: it is the plain Forest it
# became when the counter left (CR 122.1, 305.7, 611.2b). Removing no counter records no removal, so the Forest is still a land
# the Tomb mired and took no counter from, and is offered again the upkeep after.
[Bot1 Deck]
Sol Ring
Gleemox
Gleemox
Gleemox
Cyclopean Tomb
Forest
Vampire Hexmage
Disenchant
Island x30

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x30

